# Guard Patrol

entry: opening

LOCATION Harbor
  label: The Night Harbor

LOCATION Warehouse
  label: Warehouse Nine

CHARACTER Marlow
  faction: Watch
  suspicion: 0 to 100 = 10

SCENE patrol(character)
  loop
    wait until character.spotted_intruder
    -> investigate

SCENE investigate(character)
  approach
    -> examine

  examine
    wait until character.deduction > 60
    -> confront

  confront
    return clue

GENERATOR HarborChorus
  tier:     ambient
  priority: 0.3

  loop
    yield bark from Quiet night. | Stars are out. | Tide's calm.

== opening
  cast: Marlow
  setting: Harbor

The lighthouse hums.

Fog rolls off the water. Marlow's lantern swings a slow arc across the pier.

MARLOW
  (squinting into the dark)
  Harbor's closed after the ninth bell. State your business.

* Show the courier's writ.
  <set: Marlow.suspicion -= 5>
  -> warehouse_row
* Slip toward the warehouses without a word.
  <set: Marlow.suspicion += 20>
  -> warehouse_row

== warehouse_row
  cast: Marlow
  setting: Warehouse

<each visit>
  first
    Stacked crates make a canyon of the row. Somewhere ahead, a door stands ajar.
  then
    The crates again. The ajar door has not moved.

<if: Marlow.suspicion > 25>
  MARLOW
    Hold it. I know that walk — you were told to stay off the row.
  -> confronted
<else>
  MARLOW
    Warehouse Nine, end of the row. Don't make me regret the writ.

* Step through the ajar door.
  -> END
* Double back to the pier.
  -> opening

== confronted
  cast: Marlow
  setting: Warehouse

MARLOW
  (hand on the bell-rope)
  One pull and every guard on the quay comes running. Walk back the way you came.

-> END
